WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:25.770
. This is very, very fun to watch.

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:31.071
Over the last few weeks, former Democratic
presidential candidate Pete Budig Edge has

00:00:31.071 --> 00:00:38.630
been appearing on Fox News pretty often, and
he's been laying out some smack downs that

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.990
are truly a delight to watch.

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:42.740
It's just a pleasure to watch.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:45.820
It's a clinic on how to deal with Fox News.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:53.750
So Mayor Pete has been doing appearances as
a surrogate of an adviser to Joe Biden and

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:54.750
Mayor Pete.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:55.879
Has this.

00:00:55.879 --> 00:01:02.600
It's almost like a natural ability to casually
deliver hilarious and brutal attack lines

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:03.960
that you just have to see.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.270
This first one might be my favorite mayor.

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:10.369
Pete is interviewed by Fox News anchors Martha
MacCallum and Bret Baer.

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:13.130
This was on the eve of the vice presidential
debate.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:18.760
The question was, Kamala Harris and Joe Biden
have, or at least during the campaign, had

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:20.799
different views on health care.

00:01:20.799 --> 00:01:25.409
And they wanted to put Mayor Pete in a position
to have to explain or defend.

00:01:25.409 --> 00:01:26.929
Kamala has this view.

00:01:26.929 --> 00:01:27.990
Joe Biden has this view.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:28.990
How do you square it?

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:30.310
What's the right view?

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:34.619
And Mayor Pete brilliantly points out that
if you look at Trump and Pence.

00:01:34.619 --> 00:01:40.201
There is also a contrast from the primary
from, you know, between their views, which

00:01:40.201 --> 00:01:43.429
is that Pence is an evangelical Christian.

00:01:43.429 --> 00:01:46.560
And Trump is a president caught with a porn
star.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:50.780
And the looks on the faces of the Fox News
anchors are just priceless.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:55.119
Back to my original question about the things
that, you know, when you run for president,

00:01:55.119 --> 00:01:58.100
you have a record on all of these issues.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:02.069
And then we've seen that record and her stance
on them changing over time.

00:02:02.069 --> 00:02:05.210
So there's no doubt she's going to be asked
about that tonight.

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:10.960
Can you give us some insight into what she
might say to justify why she was for Medicare

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:14.520
for all then and is not for it now, for example?

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:18.970
Well, there's a classic parlor game of trying
to find a little bit of daylight between running

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:19.970
mates.

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:23.660
And if people want to play that game, we could
look into why an evangelical Christian like

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:27.520
Mike Pence wants to be on a ticket with the
president caught with a porn star or how he

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:32.630
feels about the immigration policy that he
called unconstitutional before he decided

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:34.380
to team up with Donald Trump.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.380
Folks want to play that game.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:36.380
We could do it all night.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:40.790
But I think what most Americans want to hear
about is, are our families going to be better

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:46.340
protected than they have been by this president
who's failed to secure America in the face

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:51.450
of one of the most dangerous things ever to
happen to our country.

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:56.970
You actually get the feeling that this is
fun for Pete Boutet, Judge, it's a game which

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:58.190
I have to tell you I love.

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:02.930
I've been on Fox News a couple of times, and
I also see it as a joke in a game for myself.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:05.240
I don't see it as serious journalism.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:08.590
I see it more as what can I do to make this
interesting?

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:12.660
Pete Boota judge much better than me at making
it really interesting.

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:13.910
And there's more of these.

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:16.990
Here's one where Chris Wallace tried to get
Pete booted.

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:22.300
Judge again on this primary stuff, saying,
do you stand by your criticisms of Joe Biden

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.240
when you were running against him?

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:26.300
And Mayor Pete just handles it perfectly.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:32.140
Well, what I know is we definitely need to
turn the page even more now than when I was

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:34.110
running for president a year ago.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:39.200
And what we need to turn the page from is
a president who is incapable of hand handling

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:44.820
a public health crisis that has now cost almost
a quarter of a million American lives, thrown

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:50.690
our economy into total wreckage and has clearly
no plan to do anything about it.

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:52.450
So, yeah, let's turn the page.

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:57.400
And we have a very clear choice between two
very different futures for this country and

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.020
any differences that we have.

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:03.490
Remember when everybody was was hand-wringing,
saying, how can the Democrats possibly unify?

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:05.100
Look how unified we are now.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:09.610
You've got Democrats from across the spectrum,
from the left to the center, joining with

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:13.060
independents and Republicans, because we can
all see what's at stake here.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:19.030
I mean, I can't think of an election in modern
history where the choice has been this stark.

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:21.160
And I know what side I'm on.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:28.630
What's brilliant about this and perfectly
done is that Mayor Pete goes directly at the

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:34.590
top issues for voters economy and covered
and turns the question completely around and

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:36.750
wraps it up with a bow.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:42.370
And especially if the audience was a Fox News,
you know, typical Fox News audience.

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:48.180
And they were hoping to see Pete, you know,
up against the ropes for Pete to know that

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:54.479
Trump is failing in approval on economy and
corona virus and to turn it around and to

00:04:54.479 --> 00:04:58.080
go right at those topics is absolutely perfect.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:03.550
Here is Mayor Pete calling Trump out for not
respecting his own followers by stuffing them

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:05.190
into rooms during a pandemic.

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:09.780
Look, we've seen the vice president, Vice
President Biden, campaigning across the country.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:14.749
There's one key difference, which is he's
never going to stuff his supporters into a

00:05:14.749 --> 00:05:20.379
room without masks in an indoor space over
the objections of local public health officials.

00:05:20.379 --> 00:05:26.060
When you do that, you show a level of fundamental
disrespect for your own supporters.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:29.889
So Martha MacCallum started to push back and
Mayor Pete didn't back down.

00:05:29.889 --> 00:05:30.889
Let's take a look.

00:05:30.889 --> 00:05:35.569
The point is that there's respect for the
health and safety of the people attending

00:05:35.569 --> 00:05:36.569
the event.

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:39.990
You set a certain tone when you lead people
to a certain place.

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:44.090
And if you lead people to danger, you bear
some responsibility for that.

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:47.440
In Tulsa and more recently, Nevada, he led
people into danger.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:49.099
And you know how he can tell that?

00:05:49.099 --> 00:05:53.629
You can tell what a dim view he has of the
intelligence of his own supporters was.

00:05:53.629 --> 00:05:56.580
Something they were made to do was sign a
waiver saying they wouldn't sue him if they

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:57.580
got sick and died.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:03.050
Think about what that sense for truth, for
the respect that he has very, very well done.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:05.629
And then lastly, here is Mayor Pete.

00:06:05.629 --> 00:06:07.960
This is now the day after the V.P. debate.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:11.800
He was interviewed by Fox and Friends, specifically
Steve Doocy.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:16.969
And he is going right at Donald Trump's comments
about troops being suckers.

00:06:16.969 --> 00:06:21.729
And remember, Mayor Pete is a veteran and
